---
title: "submit_application POST /v1/integration/rounds/{id}/submit (Legion Backend API)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_auth: api_key = headers["x-api-key"]
    q_auth --> q_check_key: api_key valid
    q_check_key --> q_sign: signature = HMAC_SHA256(secret_key, body)
    q_check_key --> q_reject: api_key invalid
    q_reject --> [*]: revert "unauthorized"
    q_sign --> q_send: POST /v1/integration/rounds/{id}/submit with X-Signature
    q_send --> q_parse: response = server_response
    q_parse --> q_accepted: response.status == 2xx
    q_parse --> q_round_closed: round not active
    q_parse --> q_already_applied: user already applied
    q_parse --> q_error: response.status == other error
    q_accepted --> [*]: return application_confirmation
    q_round_closed --> [*]: revert "round not active"
    q_already_applied --> [*]: revert "duplicate application"
    q_error --> [*]: revert "application failed"

    note right of q_send
        INV-001: POST body is signed (not round_id) per POST signing convention
        INV-002: user must exist before submitting application
        INV-003: round must be in active state to accept applications
        INV-004: duplicate application handling is unspecified - potential double-submit risk
    end note
